* Exercise: Images

Remember the [[⟪GTI18N_a196bc59_000001⟫][picture generator]] you wrote earlier? Let's write another one, but this time it will return an implementation of ⟪GTI18N_a196bc59_000002⟫image.Image⟪GTI18N_a196bc59_000003⟫ instead of a ⟪GTI18N_a196bc59_000004⟫ of data.

Define your own ⟪GTI18N_a196bc59_000005⟫Image⟪GTI18N_a196bc59_000006⟫ type, implement [[⟪GTI18N_a196bc59_000007⟫][the necessary methods]], and call ⟪GTI18N_a196bc59_000008⟫pic.ShowImage⟪GTI18N_a196bc59_000009⟫.

⟪GTI18N_a196bc59_000010⟫Bounds⟪GTI18N_a196bc59_000011⟫ should return a ⟪GTI18N_a196bc59_000012⟫image.Rectangle⟪GTI18N_a196bc59_000013⟫, like ⟪GTI18N_a196bc59_000014⟫image.Rect(0,`0,`w,`h)⟪GTI18N_a196bc59_000015⟫.

⟪GTI18N_a196bc59_000016⟫ColorModel⟪GTI18N_a196bc59_000017⟫ should return ⟪GTI18N_a196bc59_000018⟫color.RGBAModel⟪GTI18N_a196bc59_000019⟫.

⟪GTI18N_a196bc59_000020⟫At⟪GTI18N_a196bc59_000021⟫ should return a color; the value ⟪GTI18N_a196bc59_000022⟫v⟪GTI18N_a196bc59_000023⟫ in the last picture generator corresponds to ⟪GTI18N_a196bc59_000024⟫color.RGBA{v,`v,`255,`255}⟪GTI18N_a196bc59_000025⟫ in this one.

